        "id": 5631
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-02T19:30:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m just trying to understand the size implications here... We still have a GN variable for `skia_use_jpeg_gainmaps`, but that really just guards the XMP code (so I guess it indirectly guards anything to do with gainmaps, but no longer the multi-picture stuff). I see that our stripped-down code-size builds are growing with this, is the plan to also add the non-XMP gainmap as an always-on feature?",
      "revId": "264d0d43d5bd1c74b7be50b9ba3d0f9af038a75b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f8c608c9_0f3d1482",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 6225
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-02T19:37:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, my thought would be for the non-XMP gainmap stuff to be always-on.\n\nWe\u0027ll soon(ish) have AVIF/HEIF support, and I think it\u0027ll be more work to put that behind a flag than it would to just have it always-on. It then gets sort-of-strange to have JPEG get special treatment for the feature.\n\nI also want to further unify the JPEG metadata parsing (it\u0027s sort-of-smeared across libjpeg and the segment scanning stuff right now).",
      "parentUuid": "1babb2d0_ef0bcfcc",
      "revId": "264d0d43d5bd1c74b7be50b9ba3d0f9af038a75b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "24d4dd7b_b104f796",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 6225
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-03T08:14:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually, if you feel sort-of-iffy about the size issues, I can add the ISO stuff first behind the flag, then re-add this stuff to the build.",
      "parentUuid": "f8c608c9_0f3d1482",
      "revId": "264d0d43d5bd1c74b7be50b9ba3d0f9af038a75b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "175a3200_f63b5f8d",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5631
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-03T13:17:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That might be better - I\u0027d like to see the net size change once it\u0027s all in. In theory, the world will eventually all want gainmaps, but I suspect we\u0027re a ways off (certainly in some applications). We\u0027re not hyper sensitive to size, but we\u0027ve still got WASM clients (for example) that might care.",
      "parentUuid": "24d4dd7b_b104f796",
      "revId": "264d0d43d5bd1c74b7be50b9ba3d0f9af038a75b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
